      "creative_text": "McDonald's knows exactly how much Uber Eats and Wolt are charging your customers on top of your prices... Do you?\nWe matched 76,648 price points across every McDonald's venue in Germany - the chain app, Wolt, and Uber Eats, side by side, all 1,366 venues, all 16 federal states.\nWhat we found should be uncomfortable reading for anyone running a restaurant chain or a delivery platform in this market.\n🍟 The Happy Meal carries 4× the markup of a Big Mac.\nNot because it's worth more. Because parents don't price-check it.\n🛵 Two-thirds of the McDonald's catalogue never reaches delivery.\nThat's not a technical gap. It's a deliberate choice about who owns the customer.\n🔴 One delivery platform is missing 158 venues its competitor already serves.\nThe expansion list already exists. Someone just hasn't acted on it.\n💸 Wages swing 32% across Germany. McDonald's prices barely move.\nFlat pricing on uneven ground isn't neutrality - it's a strategic call with winners and losers.\nThis isn't a trend report. It's a breakdown of how the market leader actually prices - state by state, category by category, item by item.\nIf you set menu prices or add markup on top of them, this is what your competitors ar…",
      "library_url": "https://www.facebook.com/ads/library/?id=1723826418161486",
      "page_url": "https://www.facebook.com/doubledatacom/",
      "page_id": "",
      "link_url": "https://fooddatalab.com/food-delivery/reports/germany-mcdonalds-fast-food-pricing-benchmark?utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign=germany_mcdonalds_pricing_benchmark&utm_content=remarketing_v1",
      "link_title": "Get the full report now! We matched 76,648 price points across all 1,366 McDonald's venues in the country. Same product, same venue, every platform. The result is a benchmark that shows exactly how the market leader protects its margins - and where the food delivery apps add theirs. Here's some of what's inside 👇 🍔 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗶𝗻𝘃𝗶𝘀𝗶𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗺𝗮𝗿𝗸𝘂𝗽 Flagship items like the Big Mac carry a safe single-digit delivery premium. Kids' meals quietly carry four times that. The markup lands where customers never check the price. 🗺️ 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗰𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗴𝗲 𝗺𝗮𝗽 1,366 venues, but delivery reaches far fewer - and not where you'd expect. Hundreds of restaurants have zero presence on one platform or the other. For one side that's a blind spot; for the other, an expansion list. 🛡️ 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘂 𝗯𝗹𝗮𝗰𝗸𝗼𝘂𝘁 A large share of the catalogue never reaches delivery at all - an entire popular category is missing. That's not a platform gap. It's a deliberate decision about who controls the customer. 📈 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝗿𝗲𝗴𝗶𝗼𝗻𝗮𝗹 𝗿𝗲𝗮𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 McDonald's runs one near-flat national price while wages swing 32% across the country. Flat pricing on uneven ground leaves margin on the table - in both directions. Whether you set the menu price or add the markup on top, this is the pricing playbook of the category leader, laid out page by page. 𝗙𝗼𝗿 𝗿𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗮𝘂𝗿𝗮𝗻𝘁 𝗰𝗵𝗮𝗶𝗻𝘀: see exactly how much margin you're handing to aggregators, and where. 𝗙𝗼𝗿 𝗱𝗲𝗹𝗶𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘆 𝗽𝗹𝗮𝘁𝗳𝗼𝗿𝗺𝘀: see where coverage stops, which items carry markup, and where flat pricing costs you. 👉 Get the full report",
